
@startuml E3_API_03_MVC
title API 03: Market Trades and Conditional Order APIs (MVC view)

!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam ranksep 80
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' API interfaces based on actual routes.

package "Presentation (React)" {
  component "Trades.jsx\nportfolio/Portfolio.jsx" as UI <<View>>
  component "tradeApi.js\nordersApi.js" as Adapter <<Frontend API modules>>
}

component "Server_3 :4000 - Server_3 market trades\nPOST /api/trades/execute_trade\nGET /api/trades/get_trades" as API1 <<REST API>>

component "Server_3 :4000 - Server_3 conditional orders\nPOST /api/orders\nGET /api/orders\nPUT /api/orders/:id\nDELETE /api/orders/:id" as API2 <<REST API>>

component "Core :5000 - Core trading\nPOST /api/trade/buy\nPOST /api/trade/sell\nPOST /api/trade/execute\nPOST /api/trade/fills/:id/reverse\nGET /api/trade/fills\nGET /api/trade/fills/by-reference/:referenceId\nGET /api/trade/fills/:id" as API3 <<REST API>>

component "Core :5000 - Core internal execution\nPOST /api/internal/trade/execute\nGET /api/internal/trade/fills\nGET /api/internal/trade/fills/by-reference/:referenceId" as API4 <<REST API>>

package "HTTP controllers and application logic" {
  component "trade.controller.js (Server_3)\norder.controller.js (Server_3)\ntrade.controller.js (Core)" as Controllers <<Express controllers>>

  component "personA.gateway.js\ntrade.service.js (Core)\norderExecuter.js (scheduled job)" as Services <<Existing service modules>>
}

database "MySQL: trade_fills, wallet_transactions,\nportfolio_holdings\nMongoDB: orders, trades" as Storage

UI --> Adapter : invokes

Adapter --> API1 : market-trades
Adapter --> API2 : conditional-order requests
Adapter --> API3 : direct reversal endpoint\nPOST /api/trade/fills/:id/reverse

API1 --> Controllers : dispatch
API2 --> Controllers : dispatch
API3 --> Controllers : dispatch
API4 --> Controllers : dispatch

Controllers --> Services : calls
Services --> Storage : reads/writes
Controllers ..> Storage : direct model access where used

Services ..> API3 : gateway: POST /api/trade/execute
Services ..> API4 : scheduled order executor:\nPOST /api/internal/trade/execute

note bottom of Storage
  Database objects summarized by domain;
  this is an API interaction diagram,
  not a physical ER diagram.
end note

note bottom of Services
  A LIMIT/STOP order is stored first.
  On trigger, Core settles at market price.
  Server_3 then stores/synchronizes trade history.
end note

@enduml
